# Line endings are LF everywhere — in the repository and in the working tree, on
# every platform. Without `eol=lf`, core.autocrlf=true rewrites the working copy
# to CRLF on each checkout, and Biome's formatter (default `lineEnding: lf`) then
# flags every file it reads. CI runs on Linux, so LF is already the canonical
# form; this makes it explicit for Windows checkouts too.
* text=auto eol=lf
